# Every file in this tree ships byte-exact. No line-ending conversion, ever.
#
# This tree is a BUILT ARTIFACT: SHA256SUMS at the root records the bytes of
# every executable plus install.sh and verify.sh, and verify.sh checks them
# before anything in bin/ runs. Git's autocrlf would rewrite text files at
# checkout on Windows, which breaks that promise twice over -- the sums file
# itself gains \r on every filename (so `sha256sum -c` looks for files that
# do not exist), and the converted scripts stop matching the hashes computed
# at build time. Found on this repo's own first Windows CI run, not guessed.
#
# `-text` means "never convert", which is different from `text=false` folklore
# and from relying on every clone having core.autocrlf unset.
* -text
